<title>GREECE: GREEK BROKERS MARKET SHARE RANKINGS JAN-JULY.</title>
<headline>GREEK BROKERS MARKET SHARE RANKINGS JAN-JULY.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cumulative trading volume in the</p>
<p>seven-month January-to-July period at the Athens bourse rose to</p>
<p>5.22 trillion drachmas compared to 2.53 trillion in the entire</p>
<p>1996.</p>
<p>The Athens stock exchange members association (SMEHA)</p>
<p>provided the following market share rankings:</p>
<p>    BROKER	     VOLUME JAN-JULY	MARKET SHARE</p>
<p>			   (drs billion)</p>
<p>1.  Alpha		   451.1		    8.64%</p>
<p>2.  Sigma		   439.4		    8.41%</p>
<p>3.  National		371.3		    7.11%</p>
<p>4.  Telesis		 325.4		    6.23%</p>
<p>5.  Devletoglou	   266.5		    5.10%</p>
<p>6.  Ergo		    170.5		    3.26%</p>
<p>7.  Omega		   158.1		    3.03%</p>
<p>8.  Midland		 156.3		    2.99%</p>
<p>9.  Hellenic		133.7		    2.56%</p>
<p>10. Aspis		   131.3		    2.51%</p>
<p>11. Intersec		120.9		    2.31%</p>
<p>12. Kappa		   119.6		    2.29%</p>
<p>13. Commercial	    109.3		    2.09%</p>
<p>14. ABN AMRO Axias	104.3		    2.00%</p>
<p>15. Nuntius		 102.2		    1.96%</p>
<p>    Total volume	5,224.1</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
